---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import BreakEvenCalculator from '../../components/BreakEvenCalculator.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="Break-Even Calculator" description="Calculate how many units you need to sell to cover fixed costs, based on price and variable cost per unit.">
  <BreakEvenCalculator client:load slot="tool" />
  <h2>The core formula</h2>
  <p>Break-even units = Fixed costs ÷ (Price per unit − Variable cost per unit). The gap between price and variable cost — the contribution margin — is what pays down your fixed costs before you turn a profit.</p>

  <h2>Common mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Forgetting to include all fixed costs</strong> (rent, salaries, software subscriptions), understating the true break-even point.</li>
    <li><strong>Misclassifying a cost as fixed when it's actually variable</strong> (or vice versa), which skews the entire calculation.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Use cases</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Deciding whether a new product's pricing covers its costs at a realistic sales volume</li>
    <li>Understanding how a price change shifts the required break-even volume</li>
    <li>Explaining unit economics to stakeholders with a concrete number</li>
  </ul>
</ToolLayout>
